  {
   "bbox": [
    85.3,
    231.1,
    173.7,
    245.1
   ],
   "text": "4.1. The Incident.",
   "conf": 0.9963,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    85.3,
    258.7,
    516.0,
    274.6
   ],
   "text": "4.1.1. On October 25, 2018, at approximately 2100, the U.S. flagged, U.S. Coast Guard",
   "conf": 0.9949,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    121.1,
    272.2,
    513.2,
    289.4
   ],
   "text": "inspected, small passenger vessel PROWLER departed Mission Bay, San Diego,",
   "conf": 0.9988,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    121.1,
    286.2,
    532.7,
    302.6
   ],
   "text": "California headed south to the fishing grounds off the coast of Ensenada, Mexico for",
   "conf": 0.9998,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.7,
    300.6,
    531.1,
    316.2
   ],
   "text": "an overnight fishing charter. The vessel had twenty-three passengers for hire and six",
   "conf": 0.9977,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    121.5,
    315.0,
    237.1,
    328.1
   ],
   "text": "crewmembers onboard.",
   "conf": 0.9999,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.7,
    326.9,
    525.1,
    344.5
   ],
   "text": "On October 26, 2018, at approximately 1600, the PROWLER secured from fishing",
   "conf": 0.9983,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.7,
    342.1,
    537.5,
    357.3
   ],
   "text": "operations and began the transit north to Mission Bay with the master on navigational",
   "conf": 0.9993,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.7,
    355.3,
    535.1,
    371.6
   ],
   "text": "watch in the wheelhouse. The vessel was on autopilot with all equipment functioning",
   "conf": 0.9937,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.3,
    369.7,
    505.6,
    385.2
   ],
   "text": "as designed. At 1800, the mate relieved the master, and the master departed the",
   "conf": 0.9983,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.3,
    383.2,
    514.4,
    398.8
   ],
   "text": "wheelhouse to get some rest in his stateroom. A short time later, the mate left the",
   "conf": 0.9942,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.3,
    396.8,
    495.7,
    412.8
   ],
   "text": "wheelhouse and went to the galley to get a soda and bag of chips, leaving the",
   "conf": 0.9958,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    120.7,
    411.2,
    532.3,
    425.9
   ],
   "text": "wheelhouse unmanned and without a lookout. He returned to the wheelhouse and sat",
   "conf": 0.9974,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.9,
    424.3,
    523.1,
    440.3
   ],
   "text": "on the starboard bench in front of the helm. At approximately 1900, the vessel was",
   "conf": 0.9929,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.1,
    437.9,
    535.9,
    454.7
   ],
   "text": "passing the northwest side of Isla Coronado Norte. This prompted the mate to change",
   "conf": 0.99,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    451.9,
    533.9,
    468.3
   ],
   "text": "course to 351º, turning the vessel towards their homeport at Mission Bay, San Diego,",
   "conf": 0.9936,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.9,
    465.5,
    535.5,
    481.8
   ],
   "text": "California. Additionally, the mate adjusted the radar from three miles with a one mile",
   "conf": 0.9992,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    479.0,
    304.8,
    495.0
   ],
   "text": "ring to six miles with a two mile ring.",
   "conf": 0.9875,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.9,
    493.0,
    537.9,
    509.4
   ],
   "text": "On October 26, 2018, at approximately1800, the Cayman Island flagged, recreational",
   "conf": 0.9901,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    507.0,
    512.4,
    522.5
   ],
   "text": "yacht ATTESSA IV, departed San Diego Bay, California headed south to Puerto",
   "conf": 0.9842,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.9,
    520.5,
    532.7,
    536.5
   ],
   "text": "Vallarta, Mexico with nineteen crewmembers onboard. The master, mate and second",
   "conf": 0.9912,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    534.5,
    523.5,
    550.5
   ],
   "text": "officer were on the bridge for departure and completed a pre-departure check of all",
   "conf": 0.9882,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    548.5,
    529.5,
    564.1
   ],
   "text": "navigational and engineering systems with no deficiencies identified at that time. At",
   "conf": 0.9906,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    561.7,
    524.7,
    578.4
   ],
   "text": "approximately 1845, the ATTESSA IV cleared the entrance to San Diego Bay with",
   "conf": 0.9952,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    575.6,
    499.6,
    592.0
   ],
   "text": "the master and a lookout on watch. The master set a course of 213º using gyro",
   "conf": 0.9924,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    590.0,
    529.5,
    605.2
   ],
   "text": "steering and only using the starboard engine. The X-band (10GHz) radar, located on",
   "conf": 0.998,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    603.6,
    525.1,
    619.1
   ],
   "text": "the starboard side of the bridge, was set to eight nautical miles. The S-band (3GHz)",
   "conf": 0.9962,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.1,
    617.2,
    537.1,
    633.1
   ],
   "text": "radar, located on the port side of the bridge, was set to twelve nautical miles. At 1900,",
   "conf": 0.9967,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.1,
    631.1,
    524.3,
    647.1
   ],
   "text": "the master left the bridge to grab a snack from the galley, leaving the lookout alone",
   "conf": 0.9861,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.1,
    644.7,
    516.4,
    660.3
   ],
   "text": "on the bridge. The master returned within five minutes and ordered the lookout to",
   "conf": 0.9979,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.1,
    658.7,
    527.1,
    674.2
   ],
   "text": "conduct safety rounds of the vessel and ensure that all mooring equipment had been",
   "conf": 0.9931,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    118.7,
    672.6,
    533.5,
    687.8
   ],
   "text": "properly stowed in the bosun's locker. The master checked the S-band radar and then",
   "conf": 0.9922,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    119.5,
    686.6,
    502.8,
    701.0
   ],
   "text": "walked to the starboard side and had a seat in front of the X-band radar and the",
   "conf": 0.9891,
